{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He buried him in the valley.</b> Three signs were given for the place of Moses' burial, for it said <b>in the valley</b> — and which valley? <b>in the land of Moab</b> — and which place? <b>opposite Beit Pe'or</b>. Even so, <b>no person knows his burial</b> — to teach you that no person buried him." "<b>Until this day.</b> That no person would be buried beside him, as was done at Beit El, and that they would not inquire of the dead through him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:34.989000647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}